+### ⭐ ACTIVE (2026-07-21) — de-stale the percentile-display rules [branch `fix/metrics-display-percentile-direction`]
+
+**THIS branch = `fix/metrics-display-percentile-direction` off main @ 7419ce6. DOC PROSE ONLY — no seed, model, test, export or frontend change; zero numbers move.** Follow-up to #677 (merged), which the football-analytics reviewer flagged during that PR and which was deliberately kept out of it because these files route to a different reviewer.
+
+**The problem:** #677 gave every metric a `direction`, which made two statements in the percentile-display rules false. Both `docs/wireframes/metrics_display.md` §"Percentile display" and the screen spec `docs/wireframes/12_player_stats.md` still said (a) the player benchmark set is "11 higher_better + 7 neutral" and that for the neutral ones "top" means *most*, not better, and (b) the bar carries **no colour at all**, justified by the risk of implying a verdict on those neutral metrics.
+
+**The fix, in all three files** (`metrics_display.md`, `12_player_stats.md`, `14_team_stats.md`)**:** (a) all 18 benchmark metrics are now `higher_better` (0 neutral, 0 lower_better), so "top" reads as quality on every row and the caveat is retired; (b) the bar is **direction-aware** — green when the metric beats the median in its better direction, plain ink otherwise — as ONE bar language across every vs-population screen, player and team alike (CPO 2026-07-21, v2 design review); all three docs now state the identical rule and cross-reference each other, so the parity is real rather than asserted. Both superseded rules are recorded WITH their old rationale and why it is void, rather than silently deleted. Also corrected the ASCII mock annotation on the Duels-won row (was labelled "neutral → a lot, not good").
+
+**AMENDMENT r1:** the first draft reserved `12_player_stats.md` to a follow-up; checking it showed it repeats BOTH stale claims and it is the spec the screen is actually built from, so leaving it would be the very inconsistency being fixed (CPO: "Do I allow inconsistency?"). Pulled into scope.
+
+**AMENDMENT r2 — bi-analyst-reviewer FAIL, 4 findings, ALL upheld.** (1) **Fabricated precedent:** my r1 wording claimed the new colour rule "speaks the SAME language as the team Performance tab". No such spec exists — that name was coined for a MOCKUP in the v2 design conversation — and the only real team benchmark spec said the OPPOSITE. Citation removed; the parity is now MADE REAL by fixing the team screen in this PR rather than merely asserted. (2) **Missed staleness:** `14_team_stats.md` carried the identical defect ("10 higher_better + 5 neutral + 1 lower_better"; the true tally is **14 / 2 / 0**, and `corners_against_per_match` is now `lower_better` so it IS rank-mirrored). Pulled into scope and fixed, including its ASCII annotation and its "colour on the spread bar deferred to #366" open question, now CLOSED. (3) **Self-contradiction:** the still-live "distributional position, not a verdict" framing sat beside the new green-when-better rule; reconciled in all three files (bar LENGTH = position, bar COLOUR = whether that end is good). (4) **Missed spot:** `12_player_stats.md` §1 repeated the extinct "volume/style metric just reads as *a lot*" branch; fixed. All three files route to bi-analyst-reviewer, so the gate is unchanged.
+
+**Left alone (still accurate):** the plain-language ladder ("top X%" / "median" / "bottom X%", never "Nth percentile"), median-anchored framing, position-group peers, the 270-minute floor, the sample line, the ratio volume-triple rule, and the `lower_better` mirroring rule (still correct and still dormant at 0 such metrics).
+
+**Do-NOT:** do not touch the seed, any model, or `site_v2` here. The 26 player rows with a blank `interpretation` remain a SEPARATE sweep.
+
